---
import GenericLayout from '@layouts/GenericLayout.astro';
import Heading from '@components/Heading.astro';
import ArticleImage from '@components/ArticleImage.astro';

import MeetingImg from '@assets/about/system/meeting.jpeg';
import AsobiImg1 from '@assets/about/system/asobi_1.jpeg';
import AsobiImg2 from '@assets/about/system/asobi_2.jpeg';

const title = "System Team";
const description = "This page introduces the System Team, one of the five teams that make up TPG. The System Team is responsible for updating the TPG website and managing and operating internal infrastructure. Compared to other teams, it is smaller in size, which creates a friendly, close-knit atmosphere where members support and teach one another.";
---
<GenericLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ListItem={[
    { name: 'About TPG', path: 'about' },
    { name: 'System Team', path: 'system' }
  ]}
>
    <Heading title="Activities">
        The activities of the System Team can be broadly divided into two main areas.
        <br /><br />
        The first is website updates. The team creates and maintains content for TPG’s official website (this site), supporting publicity for events planned by the Event Team and the Community Team.
        <br />
        The second area is infrastructure management and operation. TPG uses a variety of tools to improve the efficiency of each team’s work, such as cloud storage services and chat tools. The System Team is responsible for managing and operating these tools, providing support so that members can work comfortably and smoothly.
        <br />
        None of these tasks require advanced technical skills, so even those with no prior programming experience can join with confidence.
        <ArticleImage src={MeetingImg} alt="Regular meeting" />
    </Heading>

    <Heading title="Social Activities">
        One of the characteristics of the System Team is the strong sense of camaraderie that comes from its small size.
        Members often go out to eat together after regular meetings, and sometimes even take trips together.
        <ArticleImage src={AsobiImg1} alt="Social activity image 1" />
        <ArticleImage src={AsobiImg2} alt="Social activity image 2" />
    </Heading>
</GenericLayout>
